# A NOR game whose launch fails (/torii/saves/torii is a file, so the folder
# of its save can't be made; Hello's record says Flash 128K, so there is a
# save to make): WRITE TO NOR CLEAN puts Hello.gba on the game NOR, and its launch
# (both through the menu's test hook) shows the error; after it home comes
# back whole, drawn without a key (the list stayed black until one before
# v0.3.2)
#! sd-file /torii/saves/Hello.gba/game.ini 14 tests/shots/flash128-game.ini
#! sd-file /torii/saves/torii 16 tests/roms/hello/hello.gba
#! expect-error error 2:
#! expect-error save: can't make
-w "nav: home ready"
-P "@8:nav_test_path:/Hello.gba" -p @8:nav_test_action:0x7E000003
-w "nor: list saved"
-w "nav: home ready"
-p @8:nav_test_action:0x7E000006
-w "screen ready: dialog"
-s @1:error.png
-k @8:B -k @12:-
-s @40:back.png
-s @200:later.png
